<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Frame half year headline shr flat.</title>
<headline>Frame half year headline shr flat.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			 (million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     76.0	  vs 68</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)    67.0	  vs same</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		  5.5	  vs 5.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   16.16	 vs 14.43</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   36.07	 vs 30.72</p>
<p>    Tax			 11.90	 vs 9.13</p>
<p>    Interest received	5.86	 vs 4.33</p>
<p>    Turnover		 529.55	 vs 385.46</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	1.50	 vs 0.43</p>
<p>Div payable: March 14</p>
<p>On register: March 7</p>
<p>Full name: Frame Group Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Frame chairman Mervyn King said new equipment was expected to become fully operational during the second half of the year, yielding improvements in productivity, quality and service.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
